# ============================================================================
# VPN CONFIGURATION (optional)
# ============================================================================
# Only needed if you use a vpn. Copied to /etc/vpn.conf, mode 644 root:root --
# read by firewall.sh (at boot), scripts/net and the waybar module. Separate
# from network.conf: this is provider config, not topology.
#
# INSTRUCTIONS:
#   1. sudo cp vpn.conf.example /etc/vpn.conf
#   2. Fill in the values below
#   3. net vpn      (edits it and resyncs the firewall + waybar in one step)
#
# If /etc/vpn.conf does not exist there is no vpn on this machine: every vpn
# path in the firewall stays inert and the waybar module hides itself.
#
# IMPORTANT: Do NOT commit vpn.conf (it's in .gitignore)
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIREWALL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Resolver to use while the tunnel holds the default route.
# REQUIRED if you use a vpn -- your lan resolver becomes unreachable once
# connected, so leaving this empty stops dns dead while connected. Don't trust
# the documented default; providers move it (e.g. Mullvad's DNS Content
# Blocker changes the address). Read it back instead:
#   resolvectl status | grep -iA2 'current dns'
# Example: VPN_DNS=10.64.0.1 (Mullvad) / 10.2.0.1 (Proton) / 103.86.96.100 (Nord)
VPN_DNS=

# Override for the vpn server's address and port, as "IP:PORT".
# Normally LEAVE EMPTY -- the firewall learns it from the live tunnel. Set
# only if detection fails. Space-separated for several.
# Example: VPN_ENDPOINT="185.65.135.72:51820"
VPN_ENDPOINT=

# In-tunnel address your client probes to confirm it's connected, as "IP:PORT".
# REQUIRED if your client does such a check (Mullvad does) -- without it the
# probe is denied like any other host traffic and the client gives up.
# Space-separated for several.
# Example: VPN_CONTROL="10.64.0.1:1337"
VPN_CONTROL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLIENT COMMANDS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run AS YOU by scripts/net, never by firewall.sh. UP/DOWN/MENU are invoked
# directly by `net vpon`/`net vpoff`/`net vprelay` -- the firewall switch and
# the client move together in a fixed order, so these aren't just a waybar
# convenience.

# Connect. Leaving this empty means `net vpon` flips the switch and connects
# nothing, so nothing egresses.
# Example: VPN_UP_CMD="wg-quick up wg0"
VPN_UP_CMD=""

# Disconnect.
# Example: VPN_DOWN_CMD="wg-quick down wg0"
VPN_DOWN_CMD=""

# Relay / location picker, run by `net vprelay`. Expected to CONNECT as well
# as choose -- the bundled scripts/vpn-menu.sh ends in `mullvad relay set
# location ... && mullvad connect`.
# Example: VPN_MENU_CMD="$HOME/scripts/vpn-menu.sh"
VPN_MENU_CMD=""

# What you're connected to, for the waybar tooltip. Optional -- falls back to
# the tunnel device name. Must only PRINT, never change anything; first line
# of output is used.
# Example: VPN_STATUS_CMD="mullvad status | head -1"
VPN_STATUS_CMD=""
